SelectScript:

You have a number of choices from this panel. The one
you will most likely use the most is just to select one
of the BBSs to call. To do this, just move your mouse
over the top of a name in the supplied list and push
down on the left mouse button. This will start at
Term using the indicated script.

If you are just starting off with VBBSMenu, you will
most likely wish to ADD a script to the list. (The
two supplied are VBBS - the main VBBS support BBS and
AMUC Express - the Amiga Users of Calgary BBS. If you
wish to call these BBSs you will need to CHANGE them by
adding the area code of 403 in front of the 7 digit
numbers).

To ADD a script, just select ADD from the panel. This
will take you to the Add Script panel (see it for help
in adding scripts. It's REALLY EASY!!).

To CHANGE a script, just select CHANGE from the panel.
You will then be asked to select one of the scripts
from the list supplied. Once you select one, you will
go to the Change Script Panel. (See it for further
instructions, but like ADD, you will find it VERY EASY
to change something).

For whatever reason, you might need to DELETE a script.
To do this, you need only select DELETE and then select
the script you wish deleted. It will be removed from
your list and from your disk.
